[
  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186124469,
      "id": "0096e314-e53e-5d9b-9cee-fe34fa3a6379",
      "title": "Applying the Vector Form of the Chain Rule to a Function of Two Variables"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "ab95baf6-3ac1-55ab-ae38-57db9540a03e",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "If $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2xy)$ and $\\mathbf{r}(t)={e}^{t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\mathbf{j},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))].$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))]=∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2xy))\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2xy))\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{1+4{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{2x}{1+4{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\mathbf{j}\\text{ }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x={e}^{t}$ and $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$ into the above to find $∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{1+4{e}^{2t}\\sin^{2}⁡t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{2{e}^{t}}{1+4{e}^{2t}\\sin^{2}⁡t}\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $\\mathbf{r}(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))] & =∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{1+4{e}^{2t}\\sin^{2}⁡t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{2{e}^{t}}{1+4{e}^{2t}\\sin^{2}⁡t}\\,\\mathbf{j})\\cdot ({e}^{t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\mathbf{j}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{1+4{e}^{2t}\\sin^{2}⁡t}+\\frac{2{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{1+4{e}^{2t}\\sin^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}{1+4{e}^{2t}\\sin^{2}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "176e612a-2ab0-5271-bdb9-d983256e2923",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "98416e7d-424e-53cc-ac3d-27700050416a",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{2 \\left(e^{2 t} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)}{4 e^{2 t} \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 1}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "df6c2a9e-7c1e-5fd4-93a2-6cef8bb34ffd",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{2 \\left(\\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) e^{t}}{4 e^{2 t} \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 1}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "0d080fcd-d679-55e3-aad0-eeb288c6a996",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{2 \\left(e^{t} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)}{4 e^{2 t} \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 1}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "d51719d9-0cc9-5315-9340-88f06ff3719f",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{2 e^{t} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}}{4 e^{2 t} \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)} + 1}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "c01486ce-bb0e-555f-b99c-02e1ee0ac2c1",
