    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "20c01f6a-384f-5298-a666-246713082e2c",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "If $f(x,y)=2{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}$ and $\\mathbf{r}(t)={e}^{t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+{e}^{-t}\\,\\mathbf{j},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))].$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))]=∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2})\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2})\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =4x\\,\\mathbf{i}+4y\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x={e}^{t}$ and $y={e}^{-t}$ into the above to find $∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =4{e}^{t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+4{e}^{-t}\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $\\mathbf{r}(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t})\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\,\\mathbf{i}-{e}^{-t}\\,\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))] & =∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(4{e}^{t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+4{e}^{-t}\\,\\mathbf{j})\\cdot ({e}^{t}\\,\\mathbf{i}-{e}^{-t}\\,\\mathbf{j}) \\\\  & =4{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{t}-4{e}^{-t}\\cdot {e}^{-t} \\\\  & =4{e}^{2t}-4{e}^{-2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "9b1f7a64-5889-50c0-b54f-0a37b7ed4f13",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "a64a4c29-bffb-50b9-a784-9aa75ed45a50",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "4 \\left(e^{t} - 1\\right) \\left(e^{t} + 1\\right) \\left(e^{2 t} + 1\\right) e^{- 2 t}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "674d3f6b-8b5e-5694-bc79-bf1eae7dead3",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
