    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2d08b536-0bcf-5a66-962d-2a46834d2a07",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "If $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2xy)$ and $\\mathbf{r}(t)={e}^{3t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\mathbf{j},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))].$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))]=∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2xy))\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2xy))\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{1+4{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{2x}{1+4{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\mathbf{j}\\text{ }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x={e}^{3t}$ and $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$ into the above to find $∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{1+4{e}^{6t}\\sin^{2}⁡t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{2{e}^{3t}}{1+4{e}^{6t}\\sin^{2}⁡t}\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $\\mathbf{r}(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{3t})\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =3{e}^{3t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))] & =∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{1+4{e}^{6t}\\sin^{2}⁡t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{2{e}^{3t}}{1+4{e}^{6t}\\sin^{2}⁡t}\\,\\mathbf{j})\\cdot (3{e}^{3t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\mathbf{j}) \\\\  & =\\frac{6{e}^{3t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}{1+4{e}^{6t}\\sin^{2}⁡t}+\\frac{2{e}^{3t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}{1+4{e}^{6t}\\sin^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{3t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}{1+4{e}^{6t}\\sin^{2}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
